/* book Worked example 2: Q: A 12 V battery has an internal resistance of 0.5 Ω. Find the terminal voltage, the load power and the power lost inside for loads of 11.5 Ω, 5.5 Ω and 1.5 Ω, and the short-circuit current.
   1. Model: 12 V in series with 0.5 Ω, so i = 12/(RL + 0.5) and v = 12 − 0.5i.
   2. 11.5 Ω: i = 12/12 = 1 A; v = 12 − 0.5 = 11.5 V; load power 11.5 × 1 = 11.5 W; inside loss 1² × 0.5 = 0.5 W.
   3. 5.5 Ω: i = 12/6 = 2 A; v = 12 − 1 = 11 V; load power 11 × 2 = 22 W; inside loss 2² × 0.5 = 2 W.
   4. 1.5 Ω: i = 12/2 = 6 A; v = 12 − 3 = 9 V; load power 9 × 6 = 54 W; inside loss 6² × 0.5 = 18 W. Check: 54 + 18 = 72 W = 12 V × 6 A.
   5. Short circuit (RL = 0): isc = 12/0.5 = 24 A, v = 0, and all 288 W is lost inside the battery.
   Answer: Terminal voltages 11.5 V, 11 V and 9 V; load powers 11.5 W, 22 W and 54 W; internal losses 0.5 W, 2 W and 18 W; short-circuit current 24 A. */
